<HEAD><style>/* Marginalia — page treatment sheet.
   The annotated reading copy: cream paper, warm ink, a calligraphic serif for quotations
   and a humanist sans for the reader's notes, hairline rules, two inks that each mean one
   work, one highlighter. Palette-var only — the dark swap skin flips every value through
   the theme and this sheet follows. */

.gml-card {
  --work-a: var(--palette-1);
  --work-b: var(--palette-2);
  --hairline: var(--palette-8);
  --line: 1pt;
  /* Move 8 — hairline ledger: every seam, rule, table line and cell edge is one warm hairline. */
  --grid-divider-color: var(--hairline);
  --grid-divider-width: var(--line);
  --divider-color: var(--hairline);
  --divider-thickness: var(--line);
  --cell-radius: 0;
  --cell-border-color: var(--hairline);
  --table-border-color: var(--hairline);
  --table-border-width: var(--line);
  --table-radius: 0;
  --figure-radius: 0;
  /* Numbered markers count in graphite: the two work inks never number anything. */
  --marker-color: var(--palette-7);
  /* A caption hugging a drawing keeps a line of air from its crop. */
  --caption-hug-gap: 16pt;
}

/* ─── Move 1 — quotation ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
/* A real <blockquote> whose accent bar is retired: the serif italic IS the signal. The inner
   <p> carries the size as an attr (hero 33–36pt, paired 30pt, epigraph 30pt; never below 27pt —
   the deck is sized for projection in a classroom). */
.quote.gml-blockquote {
  padding-inline-start: 0;
  margin-inline-start: 0;
  font-style: italic;
}
.quote.gml-blockquote > .gml-blockquote__bar {
  display: none;
}
.quote.gml-blockquote p.gml-paragraph {
  font-family: var(--display-font);
  font-style: italic;
  font-weight: 400;
  line-height: 1.1;
  letter-spacing: -0.005em;
}

/* ─── Move 2 — gloss ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
/* The translated line in the serif roman, set tight under its quotation so quote + gloss read
   as one object. Author it as <p class="gloss" font-size="lg">. */
.gloss.gml-paragraph {
  font-family: var(--display-font);
  font-style: normal;
  line-height: 1.22;
  margin-block-start: 4pt;
}

/* ─── Move 3 — source line ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
/* One quiet micro line under every quotation — author · work · translator · edition · page —
   separated by middle dots. Author it as <p role="caption" class="source">. */
.source.gml-paragraph {
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: 0.06em;
  font-weight: 500;
}

/* ─── Move 4 — work ink tags ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
/* The only chromatic ink on the deck besides the highlighter. A 15pt uppercase eyebrow with a
   2pt rule down its leading edge: <p role="eyebrow" class="work-a"><span text-color="accent">…
   and <p role="eyebrow" class="work-b"><span text-color="palette-2">… . */
.work-a.gml-paragraph,
.work-b.gml-paragraph {
  border-inline-start: 2pt solid var(--work-a);
  padding-inline-start: 9pt;
  margin-block-end: 6pt;
}
.work-b.gml-paragraph {
  border-inline-start-color: var(--work-b);
}

/* ─── Move 5 — margin note ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
/* The reader's analysis: a narrower sans column beside the quotation, hung from the grid's
   hairline seam, each note led by a bold keyword. Class on the note cell. */
.note.gml-grid-cell > .gml-grid-cell__content {
  --block-gap: 10pt;
}

/* ─── Move 7 — line numbers ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
/* A borderless two-column table: muted cited line numbers in a narrow gutter, the quotation
   line in the serif italic beside them. Class on the <table>. The number cell carries a <p> at
   the quotation's size with a small span inside, so both columns share one baseline. */
.lineno {
  --table-cell-padding: 2pt 16pt 2pt 0;
  --table-border-width: 0;
}
.lineno .gml-table__cell[data-col='0'] {
  text-align: end;
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}
.lineno .gml-table__cell[data-col='1'] p.gml-paragraph {
  font-family: var(--display-font);
  font-style: italic;
  font-weight: 400;
  line-height: 1.2;
  letter-spacing: -0.005em;
}

/* ─── Move 8 — hairline ledger (tables) ────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
/* References, comparison matrices, glossaries: one hairline per seam, a heavier ink rule
   under the head row only, closed by a hairline under the last row. Class on the <table>. */
.ledger {
  --table-cell-padding: 9pt 12pt;
  --table-header-color: var(--heading-color);
}
.ledger .gml-table__row[data-header] .gml-table__cell {
  border-bottom: 1.5pt solid var(--heading-color);
}
.ledger .gml-table__row:last-child .gml-table__cell {
  border-bottom: var(--table-border-width) solid var(--table-border-color);
}

/* ─── claim — the thesis voice ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
/* A <display> in the serif ROMAN at medium weight: quotations are italic, the student's own
   claim is upright. Class on the <display>. */
.claim.gml-title,
.claim.gml-display {
  font-style: normal;
  font-weight: 500;
  letter-spacing: -0.01em;
}

/* ─── prose — a measured reading column ───────────────────────────────────────────────── */
/* Running analysis paragraphs get a slightly wider beat than the note rail. */
.prose.gml-grid-cell > .gml-grid-cell__content {
  --block-gap: 14pt;
}

/* ─── spot — the drawing's cell ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
/* The cell that holds a transparent spot drawing beside type (margin spot, foot plate, act-break
   plane). It is a slot: the theme figure radius is already 0 so the cutout sits straight on the
   paper; the class marks the role so a fill writer keeps the drawing in its own cell. */
.spot.gml-grid-cell .gml-figure__img {
  border-radius: 0;
}

/* ─── voice — a tagged name cell ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
/* Work tag, name and one clause hug as a single entry inside a hairline quadrant, so four
   voices fit the frame at reading size. Class on the cell. */
.voice.gml-grid-cell > .gml-grid-cell__content {
  --block-gap: 6pt;
}</style></HEAD>
<section image-layout="blank" id="xrWcglzW6z"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="8uIczwOPpz" vertical-align="center" colspan="39"><p role="eyebrow">Vietnamese literature</p><display size="md">The Tale of Kiều:<br>Nguyễn Du and the Poem That Became a Nation</display><p><i>Truyện Kiều</i> · 3,254 lines · completed before 1820</p><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><p role="caption">Poet, plot, values, and the art of lục bát</p></grid-item><grid-item id="zsheNDwwNH" class="spot" align="right" vertical-align="end" padding="0" colspan="21"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/J5Jrtb1e0-fhu6Zbm7y5g.png" saved-media-id="dscdowvp34fs3i9" source="image.ai-generated" fill="contain" image-style="spot-line" alt="Fine pen-and-ink book engraving of a traditional Vietnamese hồ cầm stringed instrument drawn whole, its carved wooden body, pegs and strings rendered in delicate cross-hatching, one small muted teal accent on the silk tassel, clear paper around it, no person, no text, transparent background" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1248,&quot;height&quot;:1664}"></grid-item></grid><notes><p>Introduce the poem through its scale and cultural position, then name the lecture's four concerns: Nguyễn Du, Kiều's story, the poem's social and ethical values, and its native verse form.</p></notes></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="twxwivDuPO"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="DHGxar8Til"><h2>A country that tells its fortune with a poem</h2><grid divider="sm palette-8"><grid-item id="ZKwm_QsQBW" vertical-align="center" colspan="22"><p role="eyebrow">The work</p><display size="lg">3,254</display><p>lines in chữ Nôm, remembered and recited beyond the circle able to read the script.</p><p role="caption"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Truy%E1%BB%87n_Ki%E1%BB%81u">Work and date</a> · <a href="https://cand.vn/tieng-tho-lay-dong-dat-troi-post373913.html">oral circulation</a></p></grid-item><grid-item id="GqB8EdWAUA" class="note" colspan="38"><blockquote class="quote"><p font-size="27pt">“So long as <i>The Tale of Kiều</i> survives, our language survives; so long as our language survives, our country survives.”</p></blockquote><p role="caption" class="source">Phạm Quỳnh · 1924</p><p font-size="sm"><b>Bói Kiều</b> opens the poem at random to divine a fate. <b>Lẩy Kiều</b> quotes its lines; <b>tập Kiều</b> recombines them.</p><p font-size="sm"><b>This lecture’s reading:</b> Nguyễn Du inherited a Chinese plot, gave its trafficked heroine a sustained inner voice, and made her story available in a Vietnamese script and folk meter.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid><notes><p>Separate documented cultural practices from the lecture's interpretation. The practices are recorded; the claim about inherited plot, interiority, and national reading is the argument to be tested.</p></notes></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="cexNYBC-st"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="HzKXAz13yr" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow">Part one</p><display size="lg">I. The poet</display><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><grid divider="sm palette-8" direction="vertical" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="OatB2IrkY0" padding="9pt 0"><h4>A childhood inside the Lê elite</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="BDOPCyEfH9" padding="9pt 0"><h4>Two dynastic collapses</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="XBzsAWLLqd" padding="9pt 0"><h4>Service under the Nguyễn</h4></grid-item></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="uS3Qd1-yQc" class="spot" vertical-align="end" padding="0" colspan="30"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/PrrGtyDZfz9yUmgTeXPTP.png" saved-media-id="ona05aho67j7ip0" source="image.ai-generated" fill="contain" image-style="spot-line" alt="Fine pen-and-ink book engraving of an unoccupied scholar-official's long robe and folded court hat arranged on a wooden garment stand, observed in close constructional detail with delicate cross-hatching, one small dull ochre accent on the robe clasp, no person, no insignia, no text, transparent background" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1248,&quot;height&quot;:1664}"></grid-item></grid><notes><p>The biographical section keeps documented chronology separate from interpretive parallels between Nguyễn Du's public position and the poem's problem of compromised fidelity.</p></notes></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="0tP5ocLZy3"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="gDWnicns3M"><h2 font-size="34pt">He witnessed the Lê and Tây Sơn fall—and the Nguyễn dynasty begin</h2><grid divider="sm neutral-border" vertical-sizing="hug" padding="8pt 10pt"><grid-item id="bzx9FJYtqO" colspan="20"><h4 font-size="19pt"><span text-color="accent">1765</span></h4><p font-size="17pt">Born in Thăng Long</p></grid-item><grid-item id="294moNdT3z" colspan="20"><h4 font-size="19pt"><span text-color="accent">1778</span></h4><p font-size="17pt">Orphaned at thirteen</p></grid-item><grid-item id="UKP6P46jXW" colspan="20"><h4 font-size="19pt"><span text-color="accent">1786–88</span></h4><p font-size="17pt">Tây Sơn take the northern capital</p></grid-item><grid-item id="nZJQho1zc7" colspan="20"><h4 font-size="19pt"><span text-color="accent">1789</span></h4><p font-size="17pt">Later Lê ends</p></grid-item><grid-item id="-JSkaL1kTy" colspan="20"><h4 font-size="19pt"><span text-color="accent">1802</span></h4><p font-size="17pt">Nguyễn dynasty founded</p></grid-item><grid-item id="Mp50m-dnLI" colspan="20"><h4 font-size="19pt"><span text-color="accent">1820</span></h4><p font-size="17pt">Nguyễn Du dies</p></grid-item></grid><p font-size="19pt"><b>Two dynasties fell—not three.</b> After 1788 came his “ten years of wind and dust”: poor and without office.</p><p role="caption"><a href="https://scov.gov.vn/dat-nuoc-con-nguoi/nho-danh-nhan-van-hoa-the-gioi-nguyen-du.html">Biography</a> · <a href="https://www.unesco.org/en/memory-world/imperial-archives-nguyen-dynasty-1802-1945">Nguyễn dynasty, 1802–1945</a></p></grid-item></grid><notes><p>His father Nguyễn Nghiễm had reached the highest ranks of the Lê court. Nguyễn Du's father died in 1776 and his mother in 1778. The Tây Sơn displaced the Lê, then were defeated by Gia Long in 1802.</p></notes></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="aKEkcsxg_B"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="TvH4tfW3vm"><h2 font-size="30pt">He served the Nguyễn, victors over Tây Sơn—not the Lê</h2><grid spacing="large" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="YUR7KWpAMc" class="prose" colspan="20"><p font-size="18pt">The Lê line his family served had ended in 1789; Gia Long defeated <b>Tây Sơn</b> in 1802.</p><p role="caption"><a href="https://scov.gov.vn/dat-nuoc-con-nguoi/nho-danh-nhan-van-hoa-the-gioi-nguyen-du.html">State Committee for Overseas Vietnamese</a></p></grid-item><grid-item id="sEdrkzKXZe" colspan="40"><grid divider="sm palette-8" marker="number" marker-position="inline" vertical-sizing="hug" padding="10pt 12pt" style="--marker-inline-size: 22pt; --marker-gap: 8pt;"><grid-item id="cZnlwVQo8Q" colspan="30"><p font-size="18pt"><b>1802</b> · Appointed district magistrate under the new Nguyễn house.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="fQ3sB4EJ6F" colspan="30"><p font-size="18pt"><b>1804</b> · Resigns, citing illness; recalled, then rises again.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="zacObVYKI6" colspan="30"><p font-size="18pt"><b>1813</b> · Leads a Qing tribute mission; <i>Bắc hành tạp lục</i> dwells on history’s wronged and forgotten.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="raWv9Tu4IA" colspan="30"><p font-size="18pt"><b>1820</b> · Dies before a second mission.</p></grid-item></grid><p role="caption">The parallel with Kiều’s broken vows is interpretation—not evidence of Nguyễn Du’s private motives.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid><notes><p>Press the parallel only as interpretation. The archival record establishes offices and missions, not his daily motives for serving the Nguyễn.</p></notes></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="o8tD0ABsVE"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="lZBFwvPNqd" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow">Part two</p><display size="lg">II. The making of the poem</display><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><grid divider="sm palette-8" direction="vertical" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="ZWxU2oLiPC" padding="9pt 0"><h4>An inherited Chinese plot</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="CVfGdG0-uV" padding="9pt 0"><h4>A Vietnamese script and meter</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="S4AEl0OTYb" padding="9pt 0"><h4>A thesis stated before the story</h4></grid-item></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="2qmgZHDHkH" class="spot" vertical-align="end" padding="0" colspan="30"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/V_8mPRl16-3RFavapw3yE.png" saved-media-id="6syzvflgw5jl4ha" source="image.ai-generated" fill="contain" image-style="spot-line" alt="Fine pen-and-ink book engraving of a single mulberry branch with leaves and fruit drawn whole, close botanical observation in delicate cross-hatching and stipple, one small muted madder accent on one berry, clear paper around it, no landscape, no text, transparent background" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1248,&quot;height&quot;:1664}"></grid-item></grid><notes><p>The section moves from source study to Vietnamese transformation, then to the opening couplets where Nguyễn Du states the poem's argument about talent, destiny, upheaval, and pain.</p></notes></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="yf1uTNH9sK"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="1H0TcIB3er" padding-bottom="24pt"><h2>What Nguyễn Du did to his Chinese source</h2><p><i>Jin Yun Qiao</i>, or <i>Kim Vân Kiều truyện</i>, was a seventeenth-century prose romance by “Pure-Hearted Man of Talent.”</p><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><grid divider="sm palette-8" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="AybotJA6UH" colspan="20"><p role="eyebrow">Inherited</p><h4>Plot and moral frame</h4><p font-size="sm">Characters, event sequence, and the broad moral architecture come from the Chinese romance.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="cYoV2MQHfO" colspan="20"><p role="eyebrow">Disputed</p><h4>Scale of the pruning</h4><p font-size="sm">Đào Duy Anh saw no substantive addition or subtraction; other comparisons find dropped, redistributed, and compressed material.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="uoA5bVq-J3" colspan="20"><p role="eyebrow">Nguyễn Du’s emphasis</p><h4>Psychology over event</h4><p font-size="sm">The plot is inherited. On this reading, sustained interiority is his. The reunion alone occupies 526 lines.</p></grid-item></grid><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><p role="caption"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Truy%E1%BB%87n_Ki%E1%BB%81u">Source tradition and comparative accounts</a></p></grid-item></grid><notes><p>The disagreement concerns degree, not the existence of a source. All positions accept the inherited plot. The lecture's interpretive claim concerns where Nguyễn Du spends poetic attention.</p></notes></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="Xb5ZPmy6iu"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="U7ahrK9m_x"><h2>He also made it Vietnamese, not merely translated</h2><grid divider="sm palette-8" vertical-sizing="fill"><grid-item id="8cUxSteWIb" class="voice" vertical-align="center" colspan="15"><p role="eyebrow">Script</p><h3 font-size="24pt">Chữ Nôm</h3><p font-size="18pt">The demotic script carries Vietnamese at a time when Literary Chinese governs prestige and state business.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="-mt38JnyHc" class="voice" vertical-align="center" colspan="15"><p role="eyebrow">Meter</p><h3 font-size="24pt">Lục bát</h3><p font-size="18pt">The native six-eight folk form replaces the expectations of a Tang-derived court meter.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="LX5OvCBKu1" class="voice" vertical-align="center" colspan="15"><p role="eyebrow">Language</p><h3 font-size="24pt">Everyday speech</h3><p font-size="18pt">Proverbs, idioms, and social textures make the work sound Vietnamese.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="DSwMnbtkcp" class="voice" vertical-align="center" colspan="15"><p role="eyebrow">Setting</p><h3 font-size="24pt">Ming China, named</h3><p font-size="18pt"><i>“Rằng năm Gia Tĩnh triều Minh”</i> dates the fiction to the Jiajing reign, lines 9–10.</p></grid-item></grid><p role="caption">A poem in the people’s script and meter could circulate as common property rather than court property. <a href="https://vi.wikisource.org/wiki/Truy%E1%BB%87n_Ki%E1%BB%81u">Vietnamese text</a></p></grid-item></grid><notes><p>The fiction remains nominally Chinese. The Vietnamese transformation lies in linguistic medium, metrical register, diction, and social texture.</p></notes></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="Q-33uKyhOr"><grid divider="sm palette-8"><grid-item id="K_nsbjgz60" colspan="40"><p role="eyebrow" class="work-a"><span text-color="accent">Opening thesis · lines 1–4</span></p><blockquote class="quote"><p font-size="30pt">Trăm năm trong cõi người ta,<br>Chữ tài chữ mệnh khéo là ghét nhau.<br>Trải qua một cuộc bể dâu,<br>Những điều trông thấy mà đau đớn lòng.</p></blockquote><p font-size="sm" class="gloss">Within a human lifetime, <i>tài</i>, talent, and <i>mệnh</i>, destiny, seem skilled at hating one another. What the poet has seen through upheaval hurts his heart.</p><p role="caption" class="source"><a href="https://vi.wikisource.org/wiki/Truy%E1%BB%87n_Ki%E1%BB%81u">Truyện Kiều · ll. 1–4</a></p></grid-item><grid-item id="REF4TV5YHu" class="note" vertical-align="center" padding="48pt 40pt" colspan="20"><p font-size="18pt"><b>Tài mệnh tương đố</b> names the doctrine that exceptional gifts attract hostile fate.</p><p font-size="18pt"><b>Bể dâu</b>, “sea-bed into mulberry field,” figures total upheaval. Hearing recent dynastic collapse in it is a critical inference.</p><p font-size="18pt"><b>Đau đớn lòng</b> commits the poem to pain rather than detached judgment.</p></grid-item></grid><notes><p>Read the Vietnamese aloud before the gloss. The first two lines announce the talent-destiny conflict; the next two establish upheaval and the poet's affective stance.</p></notes></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="Axb4bgMo5N"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="51O3f9LbcN" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow">Part three</p><display size="lg">III. The story</display><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><grid divider="sm palette-8" direction="vertical" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="Ng4g-IM_K4" padding="9pt 0"><h4>A vow exchanged</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="UqZ_qSeIfs" padding="9pt 0"><h4>A daughter priced</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="3D6PEAbGTr" padding="9pt 0"><h4>Fifteen years trafficked</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="wr6-NvrIpB" padding="9pt 0"><h4>A reunion without repair</h4></grid-item></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="TfswfEvsvS" class="spot" vertical-align="end" padding="0" colspan="30"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/-j6LrglK-nksBds_9kl3h.png" saved-media-id="mznif544wryy8yh" source="image.ai-generated" fill="contain" image-style="spot-line" alt="Fine pen-and-ink book engraving of a traditional merchant's balance scale with several small gold pieces in one pan and the other pan hanging empty, the whole apparatus drawn in close mechanical detail with delicate cross-hatching, one small dull ochre accent on one coin, no hands, no text, transparent background" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1248,&quot;height&quot;:1664}"></grid-item></grid><notes><p>The plot section follows the changing forms of exchange: vow, family debt, purchase, coercion, state bargain, and an ending that restores kinship without erasing experience.</p></notes></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="Ww1zqunveq"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="Q4coiOWrye" padding="56pt 84pt 28pt"><h2>The vow, and the price of a daughter</h2><grid marker="number" marker-rule="true" marker-position="above" marker-align="start" marker-numbering-format="decimal-leading-zero" spacing="small" vertical-sizing="hug" style="--marker-gap: 0.6em;"><grid-item id="5bGYutQ1kf" colspan="15"><h4 font-size="23pt">Đạm Tiên</h4><p font-size="18pt">At the spring graves, Kiều mourns a dead singing-girl whose gifts and fate prefigure her own.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="pNphepEgvs" colspan="15"><h4 font-size="23pt">Kim Trọng</h4><p font-size="18pt">The young scholar and Kiều exchange a private vow before he leaves to mourn an uncle.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="NrBD7LCcIh" colspan="15"><h4 font-size="23pt">False charge</h4><p font-size="18pt">Officials threaten her father and brother. Their demand is satisfied through money.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="l_R0siZVnB" colspan="15"><h4 font-size="23pt">The sale</h4><p font-size="18pt">Kiều sells herself and asks Thúy Vân to inherit her promise to Kim.</p></grid-item></grid><grid spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="6xOvhGzcLC" background-color="surface" padding="16pt 18pt"><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="eLFtOx_6Bl" vertical-align="center" colspan="24"><blockquote class="quote"><p font-size="26pt">“Cò kè bớt một thêm hai”</p></blockquote></grid-item><grid-item id="i7vCOocK8o" vertical-align="center" colspan="36"><p font-size="18pt" class="gloss">The buyer haggles until her price settles at <i>“vàng ngoài bốn trăm,”</i> just over four hundred in gold.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid><notes><p>The opening movement joins omen, love, coercive administration, and a literal market price. Sources: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Truy%E1%BB%87n_Ki%E1%BB%81u">plot summary</a> and <a href="https://lazi.vn/edu/exercise/1546189/trong-truyen-kieu-nguyen-du-viet-trong-tay-da-san-dong-tien-dau-long-doi-trang-thay-den-kho-gi-em-hay-chung-minh-dieu-tren">sale lines</a>.</p></notes></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="y-gM6hJE5I"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="nIZq9ZMz-b"><h2>Fifteen years of being bought and sold</h2><grid spacing="large" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="AtMeq2ejea" colspan="30"><grid divider="sm palette-8" marker="number" marker-position="inline" direction="vertical" vertical-sizing="hug" padding="8pt 0" style="--marker-inline-size: 26pt; --marker-gap: 10pt;"><grid-item id="ylxFaRiiqe"><p font-size="18pt"><b>Mã Giám Sinh and Tú Bà</b> · The buyer is a procurer; Kiều is violated, sold to a brothel, refuses clients, and attempts suicide.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="MJU-aakv7q"><p font-size="18pt"><b>Sở Khanh</b> · A staged elopement and betrayal are designed to break her resistance.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="uVQA24_Uy1"><p font-size="18pt"><b>Thúc Sinh and Hoạn Thư</b> · He buys her out; his first wife has her abducted and forced into household service.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="0e7DkTUuxV" colspan="30"><grid divider="sm palette-8" marker="number" marker-position="inline" marker-numbering-start="4" direction="vertical" vertical-sizing="hug" padding="8pt 0" style="--marker-inline-size: 26pt; --marker-gap: 10pt;"><grid-item id="iueWpcY4n7"><p font-size="18pt"><b>Giác Duyên, then another sale</b> · Kiều escapes to the nun; transferred for safety, she is trafficked into a second brothel.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="Ik5DzdgxOW"><p font-size="18pt"><b>Từ Hải</b> · The rebel commander marries her and gives her authority to judge those who harmed her.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid><p role="caption"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Truy%E1%BB%87n_Ki%E1%BB%81u">Plot sequence</a></p></grid-item></grid><notes><p>Stress the changing mechanisms of control: sale, sexual violence, confidence trick, abduction, domestic servitude, renewed trafficking, and finally political power.</p></notes></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="-Vg8RA0RXF"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="GcKdE7gLOf" padding="60pt 84pt 24pt"><h2>The state is the last and worst betrayer</h2><grid marker="number" marker-size="small" marker-style="subtle" marker-shape="chevron" marker-position="above" marker-align="center" marker-fill="true" spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug" padding="0 10pt" style="--marker-chip-padding: 0.3em; --marker-gap: 0.35em;"><grid-item id="tHuc_ospOn" colspan="15"><h4 font-size="20pt">Amnesty</h4><p font-size="17pt">Hồ Tôn Hiến offers legitimacy; Kiều urges Từ Hải to accept.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="xkhgFAp7UN" colspan="15"><h4 font-size="20pt">Ambush</h4><p font-size="17pt">The promise is a trap: Từ Hải’s forces are ambushed, and he is killed.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="EhZDeak1hc" colspan="15"><h4 font-size="20pt">Victory</h4><p font-size="17pt">The commissioner makes Kiều perform, desires her, then marries her off to avoid scandal.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="jIBczfTXpy" colspan="15"><h4 font-size="20pt">Tiền Đường</h4><p font-size="17pt">She jumps into the river; Giác Duyên, forewarned, waits with nets.</p></grid-item></grid><display size="md" font-size="26pt" class="claim">Her final ruin is administered by the emperor’s lawful representative.</display><p role="caption"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Truy%E1%BB%87n_Ki%E1%BB%81u">Plot sequence and names</a></p></grid-item></grid><notes><p>This is an interpretation to press in discussion. Earlier betrayals come from traffickers and households; the final one carries the authority of lawful government.</p></notes></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="k-FB5INksC"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="RSxtkJEbim" padding-bottom="24pt"><h2>A reunion that refuses to be a happy ending</h2><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><grid spacing="medium"><grid-item id="DmGS52lI7f" border="sm solid palette-8" border-sides="top" colspan="18"><p role="eyebrow">Space given to the ending</p><display size="lg">526</display><p>lines, about one sixth of the poem.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="-KeRnQRknj" border="sm solid palette-8" border-sides="top" colspan="21"><p role="eyebrow">What is restored</p><h4>Family and vow</h4><p font-size="sm">Kim has married Thúy Vân, supported Kiều’s parents, entered office, and searched for her. The family is reunited and the marriage performed.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="6m7UaWK0Ui" border="sm solid palette-8" border-sides="top" colspan="21"><p role="eyebrow">What is not restored</p><h4>The marriage bed</h4><p font-size="sm">Kiều refuses consummation. She and Kim live as companions, honoring the vow without pretending fifteen years can be repaid.</p></grid-item></grid><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><p><b>For discussion:</b> restoration, or the poem’s admission that restoration is impossible? The refusal is hers, and the text does not explain it away.</p></grid-item></grid><notes><p>Do not treat the reunion as a quick reward. Nguyễn Du gives it more space than any single disaster and preserves Kiều's agency in determining the form of the relationship.</p></notes></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="3_JRLO_47S"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="l7YoRTauBg"><p role="eyebrow">Part four</p><display size="lg">IV. The two values</display><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><grid divider="sm palette-8" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="rRM1hFyyzN" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow" class="work-a"><span text-color="accent">Realistic value</span></p><blockquote class="quote"><p font-size="30pt">Every turn of the plot is a transaction.</p></blockquote><p>Money links bailiffs, merchants, educated traffickers, households, and the imperial commission.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="v2mbHim31y" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow" class="work-b"><span text-color="palette-2">Humanitarian value</span></p><blockquote class="quote"><p font-size="30pt">The condemned woman keeps her moral standing.</p></blockquote><p>The poem judges intention under coercion rather than treating bodily violation as guilt.</p></grid-item></grid><spacer mode="fill"></spacer></grid-item></grid><notes><p>These are critical categories rather than claims that the poem belongs to a modern political program. Realism concerns institutions and exchange; humanitarian value concerns where the poem locates moral worth.</p></notes></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="lB6_m1oDBX"><grid divider="sm palette-8"><grid-item id="1pCGnNpiZ6" padding="56pt" colspan="37"><h2>Thúy Kiều is built out of specific textual detail, not summary</h2><table col-widths="[7,53]" borders="none" striped="false" class="lineno"><tbody><tr><td><p><span text-color="muted"><span font-size="16pt">26</span></span></p></td><td><p font-size="sm"><i>“Hoa ghen thua thắm, liễu hờn kém xanh”</i><br>Flowers envy her color; willows resent her green.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><span text-color="muted"><span font-size="16pt">29–32</span></span></p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Poetry, painting, song, the five-note scale, and mastery of the <i>hồ cầm</i>.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><span text-color="muted"><span font-size="16pt">34</span></span></p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Her composition is named <i>Bạc mệnh</i>, “thin destiny,” and grieves whoever hears it.</p></td></tr></tbody></table><p role="caption" class="source"><a href="https://vi.wikisource.org/wiki/Truy%E1%BB%87n_Ki%E1%BB%81u">Truyện Kiều · ll. 26, 29–34</a></p></grid-item><grid-item id="_6wLQu3eTc" class="note" vertical-align="center" padding="48pt 42pt" colspan="23"><p font-size="sm"><b>Duty</b> · <i>Hiếu</i>, filial obligation, collides with <i>tình</i>, her vow to Kim.</p><p font-size="sm"><b>Interiority</b> · At each sale she reasons, grieves, and justifies herself.</p><p font-size="sm"><b>Fallibility</b> · She is permitted to be wrong. Her advice destroys Từ Hải.</p></grid-item></grid><notes><p>The opening description does more than certify beauty. It assigns a range of skills, names her own composition, and turns art into an omen.</p></notes></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="xNCv5oPIfD"><grid spacing="large"><grid-item id="5UnpclGPAX" padding-bottom="24pt" colspan="36"><h2>Realistic value: every turn of the plot is a transaction</h2><grid divider="sm palette-8" marker="number" marker-position="inline" direction="vertical" vertical-sizing="fill" style="--marker-inline-size: 30pt; --marker-gap: 12pt;"><grid-item id="7XmRCGE9it" vertical-align="center"><p font-size="sm"><b>Officials</b> use a false charge to extract money from Kiều’s family.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="nMV0Qo2jIa" vertical-align="center"><p font-size="sm"><b>Mã Giám Sinh</b> purchases her and transfers her into sexual exploitation.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="M5snnYrRA-" vertical-align="center"><p font-size="sm"><b>Thúc Sinh</b> purchases her release, converting one dependency into another.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="emPJR9Q2sF" vertical-align="center"><p font-size="sm"><b>Hồ Tôn Hiến</b> calculates legitimacy, victory, desire, and scandal.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="HUzSMg1wlT" class="note" vertical-align="center" padding-bottom="24pt" colspan="24"><p role="eyebrow">The poem’s money language</p><p font-size="sm"><i>“Làm cho khốc hại chẳng qua vì tiền”</i><br>The bailiffs’ cruelty comes down to money.</p><p font-size="sm"><i>“Dầu lòng đổi trắng thay đen khó gì”</i><br>Money can turn white into black.</p><p font-size="sm"><i>“Tiền lưng đã sẵn việc gì chẳng xong”</i><br>With cash in the purse, what business remains undone?</p></grid-item></grid><notes><p>The indictment is institutional. Courts, merchants, households, and the imperial commission participate. Mã Giám Sinh and Sở Khanh are educated men operating as traffickers.</p></notes></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="qn1XsOhsUj"><grid divider="sm palette-8"><grid-item id="_h-sTXxoMr" padding="84pt 36pt 60pt 84pt" colspan="35"><p role="eyebrow" class="work-b"><span text-color="palette-2">Humanitarian value · lines 3251–3252</span></p><blockquote class="quote"><p font-size="33pt">Thiện căn ở tại lòng ta<br>Chữ tâm kia mới bằng ba chữ tài</p></blockquote><p class="gloss">The root of good lies in our own heart; the word <i>tâm</i>, moral heart, is worth three times the word <i>tài</i>, talent.</p><p role="caption" class="source"><a href="https://vanhaiphong.vn/truyen-kieu-nguyen-du-phan-thu-ba-tu-cau-2885-den-3254/">Truyện Kiều · ll. 3251–3252</a></p><p font-size="sm"><i>“Có tài mà cậy chi tài / Chữ tài liền với chữ tai một vần”</i>: talent, <i>tài</i>, rhymes with disaster, <i>tai</i>.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="MiDsAx0yL6" class="note" vertical-align="center" padding="84pt 84pt 60pt 36pt" colspan="25"><p font-size="18pt"><b>Against chữ trinh</b> · The poem does not measure Kiều’s worth by bodily chastity after coercion.</p><p font-size="18pt"><b>Intention</b> · She sold herself for her father and kept her vow inwardly.</p><p font-size="18pt"><b>Wider sympathy</b> · Đạm Tiên, Từ Hải, and even Hoạn Thư receive moral attention rather than flat condemnation.</p></grid-item></grid><notes><p>Hoạn Thư's defense at Kiều's court is persuasive enough to win release. The poem's sympathy does not erase wrongdoing; it permits argument and circumstance to matter.</p></notes></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="T_OaVGrocz"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="pP6PwdQvVt" padding-bottom="56pt"><p role="eyebrow">Part five</p><display size="lg">V. The art of lục bát</display><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><grid divider="sm palette-8" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="ZTGFCUL55Q" vertical-align="center" colspan="24"><display size="md" font-size="88pt" class="claim">6 / 8</display></grid-item><grid-item id="V6W222Z7IJ" colspan="36"><h3>A native chain-rhymed meter</h3><p>Each couplet begins with six syllables and answers with eight. <i>Truyện Kiều</i> contains 1,627 such couplets.</p><p>The rhyme enters the long line at its sixth syllable, then passes forward into the next couplet.</p></grid-item></grid><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><p role="caption"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/L%E1%BB%A5c_b%C3%A1t">Lục bát structure</a></p></grid-item></grid><notes><p>The large figures name the line lengths, not a ratio. The next card demonstrates the rhyme chain and tone pattern in the poem's opening six lines.</p></notes></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="FzYAUljqlI"><grid divider="sm palette-8"><grid-item id="lrYiBNddGT" padding="42pt 30pt 28pt 54pt" colspan="40"><h2>How the six-eight line works, in the lines we just read</h2><table col-widths="[6,54]" borders="none" striped="false" class="lineno" style="--table-cell-padding: 5pt 8pt 5pt 0pt;"><tbody><tr><td><p><span text-color="muted"><span font-size="16pt">6</span></span></p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Trăm năm trong cõi người <span text-color="accent"><b>ta</b></span></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><span text-color="muted"><span font-size="16pt">8</span></span></p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Chữ tài chữ mệnh khéo <span text-color="accent"><b>là</b></span> ghét <span text-color="palette-2"><b>nhau</b></span></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><span text-color="muted"><span font-size="16pt">6</span></span></p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Trải qua một cuộc bể <span text-color="palette-2"><b>dâu</b></span></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><span text-color="muted"><span font-size="16pt">8</span></span></p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Những điều trông thấy mà <span text-color="palette-2"><b>đau</b></span> đớn <b>lòng</b></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><span text-color="muted"><span font-size="16pt">6</span></span></p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Lạ gì bỉ sắc tư <b>phong</b></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><span text-color="muted"><span font-size="16pt">8</span></span></p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Trời xanh quen thói má <b>hồng</b> đánh ghen</p></td></tr></tbody></table><p role="caption"><span text-color="accent">ta → là</span> · <span text-color="palette-2">nhau → dâu → đau</span> · lòng → phong → hồng</p></grid-item><grid-item id="C-tRD3rFE7" class="note" vertical-align="center" padding="42pt 54pt 28pt 30pt" colspan="20"><p font-size="17pt"><b>Waist rhyme</b> · A six-line ending returns at syllable six of the following eight-line.</p><p font-size="17pt"><b>Tone frame</b> · Syllables 2, 4, and 6 follow bằng, trắc, bằng. In line 2: <i>tài, mệnh, là</i>.</p><p font-size="17pt"><b>Long-line close</b> · Syllables 6 and 8 are both bằng but differ in tone: <i>là</i> is huyền; <i>nhau</i> is ngang.</p></grid-item></grid><notes><p>The rhyme chain is audible across line boundaries. “Nhất, tam, ngũ bất luận” means syllables one, three, and five are not fixed by the basic tonal rule.</p></notes></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="3GMkFFxDfW"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="4ot4FQ8tm5" padding-bottom="68pt"><h2>Why the form suits this story</h2><grid marker="number" marker-rule="true" marker-position="above" marker-align="start" marker-numbering-format="decimal" vertical-sizing="hug" style="--marker-gap: 0.35em;"><grid-item id="cpw2-k1huq" colspan="15"><h4>Folk register</h4><p font-size="sm">The meter of ca dao and lullabies.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="OaIqWeexPA" colspan="15"><h4>Across classes</h4><p font-size="sm">Composed and enjoyed beyond court culture.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="hp0ZZOHMHi" colspan="15"><h4>Rhyme hands forward</h4><p font-size="sm">No stanza break or final stop interrupts the chain.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="J-bzMQ6lDO" colspan="15"><h4>Memory carries it</h4><p font-size="sm">Interlocking sound supports recitation.</p></grid-item></grid><p font-size="sm"><b>Interpretation:</b> the unspooling form fits a life sliding from one disaster into the next. Across 3,254 lines, it places the narrative in the familiar register of songs.</p><p role="caption"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/L%E1%BB%A5c_b%C3%A1t">Form and folk tradition</a> · <a href="https://cand.vn/tieng-tho-lay-dong-dat-troi-post373913.html">Recitation</a></p></grid-item></grid><notes><p>The numbered chain represents recurrence and handoff, not a circular plot. Each rhyme closes one local unit while opening the next.</p></notes></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="XsrmqCNNRW"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="0HMcYGTeGC"><h2 font-size="32pt">Four translators, one opening: what English cannot carry</h2><table col-widths="[15,14,31]" header-row="true" borders="rows" striped="false" class="ledger" style="--table-cell-padding: 5pt 10pt;"><tbody><tr><td><p font-size="17pt">Translator</p></td><td><p font-size="17pt">Method</p></td><td><p font-size="17pt">Opening choice</p></td></tr><tr><td valign="middle"><p font-size="16pt"><b>Vladislav Zhukov</b><br>2004</p></td><td valign="middle"><p font-size="16pt">Formal meter</p></td><td valign="middle"><p font-size="16pt"><i>“Were full five-score the years allotted to born man”</i></p></td></tr><tr><td valign="middle"><p font-size="16pt"><b>Timothy Allen</b><br>2019</p></td><td valign="middle"><p font-size="16pt">Voice over meter</p></td><td valign="middle"><p font-size="16pt"><i>“It’s an old story: good luck and good looks / don’t always mix.”</i></p></td></tr><tr><td valign="middle"><p font-size="16pt"><b>Nguyễn Bình</b><br>2021</p></td><td valign="middle"><p font-size="16pt">Heroic couplet</p></td><td valign="middle"><p font-size="16pt"><i>“’Tween Fate and Talent hatred seems to reign.”</i></p></td></tr><tr><td valign="middle"><p font-size="16pt"><b>Huỳnh Sanh Thông</b><br>1983</p></td><td valign="middle"><p font-size="16pt">Blank verse</p></td><td valign="middle"><p font-size="16pt">The standard scholarly English version; the poem exists in roughly twenty languages.</p></td></tr></tbody></table><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="DTSW3BkuqM" colspan="43"><p font-size="18pt">English can preserve image, argument, compression, or patterned sound, but no English meter reproduces a Vietnamese tonal waist rhyme.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="IQiZ-nED1u" vertical-align="start" colspan="17"><p role="caption" align="right"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Truy%E1%BB%87n_Ki%E1%BB%81u">Translation excerpts &amp; editions</a></p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid><notes><p>Keep quoted excerpts short. Discuss each translation chiefly by paraphrasing the formal choice and the sacrifice it entails.</p></notes></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="t3Mcq9CAru"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="GpSdSzVXST"><h2>The afterlife of a poem</h2><p font-size="20pt">Opera, theatre, painting, film, rival states, and diplomacy repeatedly recruit Kiều for new publics.</p><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="yzOditezDg" colspan="39"><table col-widths="[18,82]" header-col="true" borders="rows" striped="false" style="--table-cell-padding: 5pt 8pt;"><tbody><tr><td valign="middle"><p font-size="16pt"><b>1924</b></p></td><td valign="middle"><p font-size="16pt"><i>Kim Vân Kiều</i>, described as Vietnam’s first feature film</p></td></tr><tr><td valign="middle"><p font-size="16pt"><b>2000</b></p></td><td valign="middle"><p font-size="16pt">President Clinton quotes Kiều in Hanoi</p></td></tr><tr><td valign="middle"><p font-size="16pt"><b>2015</b></p></td><td valign="middle"><p font-size="16pt">National commemoration with UNESCO participation</p></td></tr><tr><td valign="middle"><p font-size="16pt"><b>July 2015</b></p></td><td valign="middle"><p font-size="16pt">Vice President Biden quotes Kiều to Nguyễn Phú Trọng</p></td></tr><tr><td valign="middle"><p font-size="16pt"><b>2016</b></p></td><td valign="middle"><p font-size="16pt">President Obama quotes Kiều in Hanoi</p></td></tr></tbody></table></grid-item><grid-item id="eUx8OFGFrl" background-color="surface" colspan="21"><blockquote class="quote"><p font-size="22pt">“Trời còn để có hôm nay / Tan sương đầu ngõ vén mây giữa trời”</p></blockquote><p font-size="16pt" class="gloss">Biden’s 2015 choice: heaven has granted us this day; the mist clears and the clouds part.</p></grid-item></grid><p role="caption"><a href="https://www.bbc.com/vietnamese/articles/cjk3vxnpk0xo">Diplomatic quotation</a> · <a href="https://nguyendu.com.vn/m/vi/tong-thong-my-lay-kieu-qua-ban-dich-nao--33F1C684D865596DB82A31C0E3BEFA31.html">Reported translation history</a></p></grid-item></grid><notes><p>Under French rule the poem was used to demonstrate Vietnamese as a literary language. North, South, and the unified state later interpreted it in different political frames. Clinton chose lines on lotus, chrysanthemum, winter, and spring.</p></notes></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="PlX7tfbdqE"><grid divider="sm palette-8" padding="40pt 44pt"><grid-item id="iOlsgwtLwd" vertical-align="center" colspan="36"><p role="eyebrow" class="work-a"><span text-color="accent">The actual final couplet · lines 3253–3254</span></p><blockquote class="quote"><p font-size="32pt">Lời quê chắp nhặt dông dài<br>Mua vui cũng được một vài trống canh</p></blockquote><p font-size="18pt" class="gloss">Rustic words strung together at length, good for a few hours’ amusement.</p><p role="caption" class="source"><a href="https://vanhaiphong.vn/truyen-kieu-nguyen-du-phan-thu-ba-tu-cau-2885-den-3254/">Truyện Kiều · ll. 3253–3254</a></p></grid-item><grid-item id="PXGzhCyNyS" class="note" vertical-align="center" colspan="24"><h2 font-size="30pt">Nguyễn Du expected to be forgotten</h2><p font-size="18pt">The modesty was conventional. The estimate was wrong: the poem became oracle, national symbol, and diplomatic language.</p><p font-size="18pt">He inherited a plot and supplied a consciousness; wrote in the people’s script and meter; and held that a woman sold twice into a brothel had kept her honor.</p><display size="md" font-size="29pt" class="claim"><i>Tâm</i> outweighs <i>tài</i>.</display></grid-item></grid><notes><p>The tâm and tài couplet is penultimate, not final. End on the modest envoi, then return to the lecture's claim: moral intention under coercion outweighs talent, status, and bodily circumstance.</p></notes></section>